{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and Marco's First Argument", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Where She Went", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Let's compare the simple past and present perfect:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span>  <br>It refers to an action that occurred at a definite time in the past.   <br><br>Examples:  <br>I said things that I didn't mean yesterday. <br>He caught me at a bad time last Saturday. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " These actions are finished when we have a definite time (yesterday, last Saturday).<br><br>  You can use other time expressions + simple past", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He did that ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in 2000<br>                                         last night<br>                                         last weekend<br>                                         on January 2nd<br>                                          three days ago\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span><br><br>It refers to an action that happened at an indefinite time in the past.<br><br>  Examples:  <br/>You guys have always made up and moved on.<br>  I have said terrible things.<br><br>  These actions can continue to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We have talked about getting married ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for years.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We have been a couple ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since 2014.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have waited for Vanessa ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since she took off.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"never taken her suitcases.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you talk about routines in the past, you can use the expressions <span class=\"strong\">would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>, followed by the verb in the basic form.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You used to talk about how you and her are going to get married. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You would always come over and blow off steam at my place, right? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you use the expression <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> in the negative form, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">did</span>. Look at the change in the expression:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">You used to talk about how you two are going to get married.<br/> I used to count on you.<br/> I didn't use to talk to anybody else.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> for the negative form of the expression:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">We would talk about our future plans. <br/>We wouldn't spend time fighting at all.</span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to catch someone at a bad time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to interrupt someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did I catch you at a bad time?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about an argument.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to mess it up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to ruin something good or a good situation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've really messed it up this time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to move on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stop dealing with something or someone and do something else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You guys always made up and moved on.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to cool off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to calm down", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You would always come to my house to cool off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stupid", "type": "name"}, {"content": "foolish", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't believe how stupid I am! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to be hard on yourself ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to tell yourself negative things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't be so hard on yourself. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Discuss with your partner what you do (or did) to blow off steam.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare which method works best.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask follow-up questions to keep the conversation going.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I discuss with my partner what I do to blow off steam.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what I used to do to blow off steam.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask follow-up questions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le12ob10re2img06.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le12ob10re2img06.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tony</span>: Hello? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Hi, Tony ... it's Marco. Did I catch you at a bad time?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tony</span>: Not at all. I thought you were in Cambridge, visiting Vanessa. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: I am. I've messed it all up, Tony!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tony</span>: What do you mean? You used to talk about how you two are going to get married. What happened?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: I've behaved terribly ... I said things that I didn't mean."}, {"image": "engenn6le12ob10re2img06.jpg", "time": "21500", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tony</span>: Where's Vanessa? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: I don't know where she went. She took off with a suitcase and her phone. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tony</span>: OK, don't worry. You guys have always made up and moved on, right?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Yeah \u2026<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tony</span>: She just needs time to cool off. You would always come 